id: pm-gh1391
title: "GH-1391: Express faithful self-isolating source package gates without tracker redirects"
description: The reporter needs source-workspace package acceptance without inherited PM_PATH while current none-mode requires an isolated or snapshot workspace. Existing source-tracker safety and trust rules must remain enforced; no new source bypass is assumed safe.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-04T11:46:01.044Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-08T06:31:11.350Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-08T06:31:10.681Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-08T06:31:10.681Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: Reproduce the nested disposable SDK-root failure and snapshot identity gap; Define an explicit source-tracker protection contract before permitting source execution without PM_PATH; Preserve PM_GLOBAL_PATH isolation and trust checks; Real package commands match direct CI results without mutating the source tracker.
goal: project management = context management
objective: Trustworthy bounded context and SDK-owned evidence
value: Agents can act on one truthful context read and preserve durable evidence
parent: pm-ugqx
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: "Disposable snapshots preserve independent Git HEAD and tags with an explicit removable origin remote, original nested dependency paths and safe fixture Git environments."
expected_result: Tag-aware package gates and nested disposable initialization work across supported runtimes without source-tracker or Git-selector writeback.
actual_result: "Real custom clone-default and inherited-GIT_DIR controls fail before their fixes and pass afterward; the inherited repository directory stays absent. Node 22 linked Git acceptance and 22 Node 24 focused cases pass, and packed SDK journeys with the custom preference pass Node 22/24/26 and Bun. All first-head hosted checks and local static aggregate pass; updated-head review and CI remain required before merge."
affected_version: 2026.10.4
